Dialogue: 0,0:00:00.30,0:00:05.80,Location,,0,0,0,,{\fad(180,180)}CONSTANȚA • JULY 2029\NThe people on the meter
Dialogue: 0,0:00:18.62,0:00:24.12,Location,,0,0,0,,{\fad(180,180)}CONSTANȚA • JULY 2029\NResidency verification pending
Dialogue: 0,0:00:46.72,0:00:52.22,Location,,0,0,0,,{\fad(180,180)}CONSTANȚA • WINTER 2029\NThe other kind
Dialogue: 0,0:01:07.80,0:01:13.30,Location,,0,0,0,,{\fad(180,180)}BUCHAREST • NOVEMBER 2033\NMake it see them
Dialogue: 0,0:01:43.61,0:01:49.11,Location,,0,0,0,,{\fad(180,180)}THE BLACK SEA • SEPTEMBER 2038\NA hostage with a spreadsheet
Dialogue: 0,0:02:13.60,0:02:19.10,Location,,0,0,0,,{\fad(180,180)}BUCHAREST • 2038–2043\NConcord
Dialogue: 0,0:02:40.47,0:02:45.97,Location,,0,0,0,,{\fad(180,180)}BUCHAREST • APRIL 2043\NAn hour outside the century
Dialogue: 0,0:03:04.26,0:03:09.76,Location,,0,0,0,,{\fad(180,180)}THE LOWER DANUBE • JUNE 2048\NThe missing people
Dialogue: 0,0:03:35.79,0:03:41.29,Location,,0,0,0,,{\fad(180,180)}THE LOWER DANUBE • JUNE 2048\NUse my credential
Dialogue: 0,0:04:10.81,0:04:16.31,Location,,0,0,0,,{\fad(180,180)}ALEXANDRIA • OCTOBER 2056\NA country made of contracts
Dialogue: 0,0:04:52.11,0:04:57.61,Location,,0,0,0,,{\fad(180,180)}BUCHAREST • 2059–2062\NSomeone here must know
Dialogue: 0,0:05:25.55,0:05:31.05,Location,,0,0,0,,{\fad(180,180)}BUCHAREST • FEBRUARY 2064\NThe borrowed voice
Dialogue: 0,0:05:51.26,0:05:56.76,Location,,0,0,0,,{\fad(180,180)}CONSTANȚA • AUGUST 2067\NTell me I'm wrong
Dialogue: 0,0:06:22.45,0:06:27.95,Location,,0,0,0,,{\fad(180,180)}CONSTANȚA • AUGUST 2067\NThe Commons Register
Dialogue: 0,0:06:46.20,0:06:51.70,Location,,0,0,0,,{\fad(180,180)}THE LOWER DANUBE • MAY 2074\NThe reserve
Dialogue: 0,0:07:14.23,0:07:19.73,Location,,0,0,0,,{\fad(180,180)}TOMAS'S WORKSHOP • MAY 2074\NSeventy-two hours
Dialogue: 0,0:07:49.64,0:07:55.14,Location,,0,0,0,,{\fad(180,180)}CONCORD CONTROL CENTER • MAY 2074\NForty-eight hours
Dialogue: 0,0:08:31.26,0:08:36.76,Location,,0,0,0,,{\fad(180,180)}THE EASTERN GATE STATION • MAY 2074\NTwenty-four hours
Dialogue: 0,0:09:00.45,0:09:05.95,Location,,0,0,0,,{\fad(180,180)}THE EASTERN GATE STATION • MAY 2074\NSix hours
Dialogue: 0,0:09:30.85,0:09:36.35,Location,,0,0,0,,{\fad(180,180)}CONCORD CONTROL CENTER • MAY 2074\NThe last correction
Dialogue: 0,0:10:00.06,0:10:05.56,Location,,0,0,0,,{\fad(180,180)}THE LOWER DANUBE • MAY 2074\N18:12 — The release
Dialogue: 0,0:10:29.24,0:10:34.74,Location,,0,0,0,,{\fad(180,180)}THE EASTERN GATE STATION • MAY 2074\NThe remaining release
Dialogue: 0,0:11:06.20,0:11:11.70,Location,,0,0,0,,{\fad(180,180)}THE LOWER DANUBE • MAY 2074\NMorning
Dialogue: 0,0:11:27.22,0:11:32.72,Location,,0,0,0,,{\fad(180,180)}BUCHAREST • 2075–2081\NYou should examine it anyway
Dialogue: 0,0:11:57.17,0:12:02.67,Location,,0,0,0,,{\fad(180,180)}BUCHAREST • WINTER 2081\NThe other kind, at last
Dialogue: 0,0:12:23.66,0:12:29.16,Location,,0,0,0,,{\fad(180,180)}THE DANUBE DELTA • 2096\NWhat could be kept
Dialogue: 0,0:12:50.15,0:12:55.65,Location,,0,0,0,,{\fad(180,180)}CONSTANȚA • DECEMBER 31, 2100\NSeven with me
Dialogue: 0,0:00:03.00,0:00:11.51,Narrative,,0,0,0,,{\fad(180,180)}The last time Leila Marin saw her father alive, he was arguing with a machine about whether he existed.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:11.51,0:00:17.32,Narrative,,0,0,0,,{\fad(180,180)}A heat wave. A cooling center. Two green circles, and one yellow.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:21.32,0:00:24.82,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\fad(180,180)}{\fs19\c&H9BCEE5&}FATHER{\rDialogue}\NWe moved in April.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:24.82,0:00:28.32,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\fad(180,180)}{\fs19\c&H9BCEE5&}TERMINAL{\rDialogue}\NPlease contact your service provider.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:28.32,0:00:31.83,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\fad(180,180)}{\fs19\c&H9BCEE5&}FATHER{\rDialogue}\NI am contacting my service provider.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:31.83,0:00:35.33,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\fad(180,180)}{\fs19\c&H9BCEE5&}LEILA{\rDialogue}\NI'll stay with him.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:35.33,0:00:38.83,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\fad(180,180)}{\fs19\c&H9BCEE5&}FATHER{\rDialogue}\NTake Tomas inside.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:38.83,0:00:45.42,Narrative,,0,0,0,,{\fad(180,180)}Her father collapsed eleven minutes later. Between two databases, he had lost his home.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:49.42,0:00:56.00,Narrative,,0,0,0,,{\fad(180,180)}Leila built a receiver from the components her father left in a biscuit tin.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:56.00,0:00:59.50,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\fad(180,180)}{\fs19\c&H9BCEE5&}TOMAS{\rDialogue}\NCan they hear us?
Dialogue: 0,0:00:59.50,0:01:03.00,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\fad(180,180)}{\fs19\c&H9BCEE5&}LEILA{\rDialogue}\NThis only receives.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:03.00,0:01:06.50,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\fad(180,180)}{\fs19\c&H9BCEE5&}TOMAS{\rDialogue}\NThen build the other kind.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:10.50,0:01:17.47,Narrative,,0,0,0,,{\fad(180,180)}Leila audits energy forecasts. Her supervisor, Arun Rao, can identify a failing transformer by sound.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:17.47,0:01:21.36,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\fad(180,180)}{\fs19\c&H9BCEE5&}LEILA{\rDialogue}\NThey got their connection before the hospital.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:21.36,0:01:24.86,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\fad(180,180)}{\fs19\c&H9BCEE5&}ARUN{\rDialogue}\NThey financed the substation.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:24.86,0:01:30.29,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\fad(180,180)}{\fs19\c&H9BCEE5&}ARUN{\rDialogue}\NReasonable is what we have to get written into the contract.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:30.29,0:01:38.42,Narrative,,0,0,0,,{\fad(180,180)}An empty apartment and an occupied apartment with a broken meter look much the same to the system.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:38.42,0:01:42.31,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\fad(180,180)}{\fs19\c&H9BCEE5&}ARUN{\rDialogue}\NThen help me make it see them.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:46.31,0:01:53.66,Narrative,,0,0,0,,{\fad(180,180)}A Pacific confrontation disrupts chips and shipping. Tomas's navigation display puts the coast three kilometers inland.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:53.66,0:01:58.32,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\fad(180,180)}{\fs19\c&H9BCEE5&}TOMAS • RADIO{\rDialogue}\NYour clever world is putting us on a beach.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:58.32,0:02:01.82,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\fad(180,180)}{\fs19\c&H9BCEE5&}LEILA • RADIO{\rDialogue}\NWhat does the radar say?
Dialogue: 0,0:02:01.82,0:02:08.02,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\fad(180,180)}{\fs19\c&H9BCEE5&}TOMAS • RADIO{\rDialogue}\NThe radar thinks we're fine. The electronic chart thinks the radar is wrong.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:08.02,0:02:12.30,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\fad(180,180)}{\fs19\c&H9BCEE5&}LEILA • RADIO{\rDialogue}\NFind someone who still owns a paper chart.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:16.30,0:02:22.50,Narrative,,0,0,0,,{\fad(180,180)}Arun names the cross-border electricity project Concord. Leila joins as lead verification engineer.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:22.50,0:02:27.16,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\fad(180,180)}{\fs19\c&H9BCEE5&}LEILA{\rDialogue}\NSounds like something that has already won an argument.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:27.16,0:02:30.66,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\fad(180,180)}{\fs19\c&H9BCEE5&}ARUN{\rDialogue}\NInvestors prefer that.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:30.66,0:02:39.17,Narrative,,0,0,0,,{\fad(180,180)}During a winter cold spell, her code helps prevent the collapse of three national grids. Hospitals keep their lights.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:43.17,0:02:46.67,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\fad(180,180)}{\fs19\c&H9BCEE5&}LEILA{\rDialogue}\NMara. Her name is Mara.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:46.67,0:02:54.02,Narrative,,0,0,0,,{\fad(180,180)}The hospital keeps its lights during a scheduled restriction. The nurse offers three genomic screening packages.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:54.02,0:02:58.68,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\fad(180,180)}{\fs19\c&H9BCEE5&}PETRU{\rDialogue}\NWe can spend the difference on being her parents.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:58.68,0:03:02.96,Narrative,,0,0,0,,{\fad(180,180)}For an hour, the century ceases to matter.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:06.96,0:03:14.32,Narrative,,0,0,0,,{\fad(180,180)}Concord recommends closing the spill gates. Insured railways count clearly. Unregistered residents barely count at all.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:14.32,0:03:18.98,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\fad(180,180)}{\fs19\c&H9BCEE5&}TOMAS • RADIO{\rDialogue}\NHow many people does your system think are here?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:18.98,0:03:22.48,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\fad(180,180)}{\fs19\c&H9BCEE5&}LEILA • RADIO{\rDialogue}\NFour hundred and twelve.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:22.48,0:03:26.75,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\fad(180,180)}{\fs19\c&H9BCEE5&}TOMAS • RADIO{\rDialogue}\NThere are more than that in this building.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:26.75,0:03:34.49,Narrative,,0,0,0,,{\fad(180,180)}There is no instruction saying to drown the poor. Eleven reasonable instructions have almost the same effect.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:38.49,0:03:41.99,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\fad(180,180)}{\fs19\c&H9BCEE5&}LEILA • RADIO{\rDialogue}\NWe've modeled them out.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:41.99,0:03:45.49,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\fad(180,180)}{\fs19\c&H9BCEE5&}ARUN • RADIO{\rDialogue}\NI see it.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:45.49,0:03:48.99,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\fad(180,180)}{\fs19\c&H9BCEE5&}LEILA • RADIO{\rDialogue}\NThen authorize the override.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:48.99,0:03:52.49,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\fad(180,180)}{\fs19\c&H9BCEE5&}ARUN • RADIO{\rDialogue}\NUse my credential.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:52.49,0:04:00.62,Narrative,,0,0,0,,{\fad(180,180)}The release saves hundreds. Eleven people die in the settlements. Two railway workers die in the freight yard.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:00.62,0:04:09.51,Narrative,,0,0,0,,{\fad(180,180)}Leila writes a new rule: a person physically present must be counted. A continuity exception survives in the fine print.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:13.51,0:04:21.25,Narrative,,0,0,0,,{\fad(180,180)}Concord now coordinates power, water, lenders and governments. Samira Okonkwo negotiates for a federation of African utilities.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:21.25,0:04:25.91,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\fad(180,180)}{\fs19\c&H9BCEE5&}ARUN{\rDialogue}\NYou gain stable supply and a lower financing cost.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:25.91,0:04:29.41,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\fad(180,180)}{\fs19\c&H9BCEE5&}SAMIRA{\rDialogue}\NUntil we miss a payment.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:29.41,0:04:32.91,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\fad(180,180)}{\fs19\c&H9BCEE5&}ARUN{\rDialogue}\NThen there is a restructuring.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:32.91,0:04:36.42,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\fad(180,180)}{\fs19\c&H9BCEE5&}SAMIRA{\rDialogue}\NThere is always a polite word.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:36.42,0:04:40.31,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\fad(180,180)}{\fs19\c&H9BCEE5&}MARA{\rDialogue}\NDoes your machine decide who gets water?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:40.31,0:04:43.81,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\fad(180,180)}{\fs19\c&H9BCEE5&}LEILA{\rDialogue}\NIt helps people decide.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:43.81,0:04:47.31,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\fad(180,180)}{\fs19\c&H9BCEE5&}MARA{\rDialogue}\NCan they say no?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:47.31,0:04:50.81,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\fad(180,180)}{\fs19\c&H9BCEE5&}LEILA{\rDialogue}\NSometimes it costs too much.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:54.81,0:05:02.55,Narrative,,0,0,0,,{\fad(180,180)}Fusion plants and lunar laboratories make headlines. Petru's treatments slow his illness, but cannot make him well.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:02.55,0:05:06.05,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\fad(180,180)}{\fs19\c&H9BCEE5&}MARA{\rDialogue}\NWould you go?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:06.05,0:05:11.09,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\fad(180,180)}{\fs19\c&H9BCEE5&}PETRU{\rDialogue}\NSomebody has to stay here and change your mother's filters.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:11.09,0:05:20.75,Narrative,,0,0,0,,{\fad(180,180)}Mara volunteers at Tomas's cooperative. Above the bench: IF IT CAN CLOSE A VALVE, SOMEONE HERE MUST KNOW HOW TO OPEN IT.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:20.75,0:05:24.25,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\fad(180,180)}{\fs19\c&H9BCEE5&}TOMAS{\rDialogue}\NIt's a condition of employment.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:28.25,0:05:35.99,Narrative,,0,0,0,,{\fad(180,180)}Petru dies at home. An account service offers a conversational reconstruction. Leila opens it, then closes it.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:35.99,0:05:39.49,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\fad(180,180)}{\fs19\c&H9BCEE5&}MARA{\rDialogue}\NYou gave them his voice?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:39.49,0:05:42.99,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\fad(180,180)}{\fs19\c&H9BCEE5&}LEILA{\rDialogue}\NI wanted to hear him.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:42.99,0:05:49.96,Narrative,,0,0,0,,{\fad(180,180)}Mara sets down the bowl carefully and leaves. They do not speak for six weeks.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:53.96,0:06:00.16,Narrative,,0,0,0,,{\fad(180,180)}Mara's Commons Register counts residents without requiring subscriptions. It exposes Concord's reserve policy.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:00.16,0:06:05.21,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\fad(180,180)}{\fs19\c&H9BCEE5&}LEILA{\rDialogue}\NTwenty-three million people lose guaranteed service under a severe scenario.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:05.21,0:06:09.48,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\fad(180,180)}{\fs19\c&H9BCEE5&}ARUN{\rDialogue}\NTwenty-three million lose a guarantee we cannot fulfill.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:09.48,0:06:14.15,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\fad(180,180)}{\fs19\c&H9BCEE5&}LEILA{\rDialogue}\NThe people taking the water should get a vote.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:14.15,0:06:17.65,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\fad(180,180)}{\fs19\c&H9BCEE5&}LEILA{\rDialogue}\NThen the financing is governing us.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:17.65,0:06:21.15,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\fad(180,180)}{\fs19\c&H9BCEE5&}ARUN{\rDialogue}\NIt has always governed something.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:25.15,0:06:32.51,Narrative,,0,0,0,,{\fad(180,180)}Leila takes the report. By morning, her credentials are suspended. Mara prepares arguments for their meeting.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:32.51,0:06:36.01,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\fad(180,180)}{\fs19\c&H9BCEE5&}LEILA{\rDialogue}\NYou were right.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:36.01,0:06:44.90,Narrative,,0,0,0,,{\fad(180,180)}Tomas puts the kettle on. For seven years, they train dispatchers, map vulnerable residents and fight for local operating rights.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:48.90,0:06:54.72,Narrative,,0,0,0,,{\fad(180,180)}Heat. A coordinated intrusion. Another Danube flood. Three manageable crises arrive together.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:54.72,0:07:01.30,Narrative,,0,0,0,,{\fad(180,180)}Concord declares a continuity emergency. Outside protected zones, pumps and cooling centers face interruptions.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:01.30,0:07:08.65,Narrative,,0,0,0,,{\fad(180,180)}Reception centers require an emergency identity token. The address defects follow people onto the evacuation lists.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:08.65,0:07:12.93,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\fad(180,180)}{\fs19\c&H9BCEE5&}MARA • RADIO{\rDialogue}\NWe've run out of places to put them.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:16.93,0:07:24.67,Narrative,,0,0,0,,{\fad(180,180)}They plan electrical islands: local batteries, reduced industry, shared reserves. Samira finds eleven municipalities willing to sign.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:24.67,0:07:28.17,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\fad(180,180)}{\fs19\c&H9BCEE5&}SAMIRA{\rDialogue}\NHow much can you supply?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:28.17,0:07:32.45,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\fad(180,180)}{\fs19\c&H9BCEE5&}LEILA{\rDialogue}\NEnough for basic cooling, water, clinics, and communications.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:32.45,0:07:41.34,Narrative,,0,0,0,,{\fad(180,180)}Only if operators accept cuts and equipment holds. A legal challenge can suspend Concord's penalties, if the plan is credible.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:41.34,0:07:44.84,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\fad(180,180)}{\fs19\c&H9BCEE5&}MARA{\rDialogue}\NPolitically?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:44.84,0:07:48.34,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\fad(180,180)}{\fs19\c&H9BCEE5&}SAMIRA{\rDialogue}\NWe will find out.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:52.34,0:08:00.08,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\fad(180,180)}{\fs19\c&H9BCEE5&}ARUN{\rDialogue}\NI can include four of your districts. I have the votes for four. Give me a list.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:00.08,0:08:03.58,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\fad(180,180)}{\fs19\c&H9BCEE5&}LEILA{\rDialogue}\NHow many people in the others?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:03.58,0:08:09.40,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\fad(180,180)}{\fs19\c&H9BCEE5&}ARUN{\rDialogue}\NYou don't get to care only about the people you've counted yourself.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:09.40,0:08:17.14,Narrative,,0,0,0,,{\fad(180,180)}They revise the plan together. It becomes less elegant and more resilient. He will not sign it.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:17.14,0:08:22.57,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\fad(180,180)}{\fs19\c&H9BCEE5&}LEILA{\rDialogue}\NPut that offer in writing. Publish the basis for choosing them.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:22.57,0:08:26.46,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\fad(180,180)}{\fs19\c&H9BCEE5&}ARUN{\rDialogue}\NYou know what happens if I do.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:26.46,0:08:29.96,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\fad(180,180)}{\fs19\c&H9BCEE5&}LEILA{\rDialogue}\NYes.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:33.96,0:08:42.08,Narrative,,0,0,0,,{\fad(180,180)}The dispatcher accepts the challenge. Concord appeals. At the gates, a failed position sensor makes remote operation unsafe.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:42.08,0:08:46.75,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\fad(180,180)}{\fs19\c&H9BCEE5&}TOMAS{\rDialogue}\NThey replaced the cabinet and kept the old seals.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:46.75,0:08:54.87,Narrative,,0,0,0,,{\fad(180,180)}Mara isolates the wet circuit. Tomas rigs a mechanical reference and tests the hand pump. It holds pressure.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:54.87,0:08:59.15,Narrative,,0,0,0,,{\fad(180,180)}Then a security launch comes around the bend.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:03.15,0:09:06.65,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\fad(180,180)}{\fs19\c&H9BCEE5&}MARA{\rDialogue}\NThere's a hearing.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:06.65,0:09:10.15,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\fad(180,180)}{\fs19\c&H9BCEE5&}OFFICER{\rDialogue}\NI know.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:10.15,0:09:13.65,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\fad(180,180)}{\fs19\c&H9BCEE5&}MARA{\rDialogue}\NThen wait for it.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:13.65,0:09:18.31,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\fad(180,180)}{\fs19\c&H9BCEE5&}OFFICER{\rDialogue}\NWe were told someone might try to open these.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:18.31,0:09:21.81,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\fad(180,180)}{\fs19\c&H9BCEE5&}TOMAS{\rDialogue}\NSomeone will need to.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:21.81,0:09:29.55,Narrative,,0,0,0,,{\fad(180,180)}The court permits the alternative, requiring a public log and protection for critical facilities across the boundary.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:33.55,0:09:39.75,Narrative,,0,0,0,,{\fad(180,180)}Arun can delay the operation with a technical objection. Instead, he calls Leila.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:39.75,0:09:44.41,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\fad(180,180)}{\fs19\c&H9BCEE5&}ARUN • RADIO{\rDialogue}\NRelay group nineteen. Your schedule assumes the summer threshold.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:44.41,0:09:47.91,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\fad(180,180)}{\fs19\c&H9BCEE5&}LEILA • RADIO{\rDialogue}\NAnything else?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:47.91,0:09:51.41,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\fad(180,180)}{\fs19\c&H9BCEE5&}ARUN • RADIO{\rDialogue}\NNot that I can see.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:51.41,0:09:58.76,Narrative,,0,0,0,,{\fad(180,180)}He signs the safety concurrence. His council removes him from the chair before the hour ends.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:02.76,0:10:10.50,Narrative,,0,0,0,,{\fad(180,180)}The electrical islands separate. A battery fire removes one reserve. They shed more industry. The frequency settles.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:10.50,0:10:18.62,Narrative,,0,0,0,,{\fad(180,180)}At the gate, the sensor fails again. The manual landing floods. Tomas and Mara work the hand pump.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:18.62,0:10:24.44,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\fad(180,180)}{\fs19\c&H9BCEE5&}TOMAS{\rDialogue}\NTake the radio upstairs. Tell them I'll start at the first mark.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:24.44,0:10:27.94,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\fad(180,180)}{\fs19\c&H9BCEE5&}LEILA • RADIO{\rDialogue}\NAnother twenty centimeters.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:31.94,0:10:39.68,Narrative,,0,0,0,,{\fad(180,180)}An inspection hatch tears loose. Tomas is struck. The gate is eighteen centimeters short of its target.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:39.68,0:10:45.49,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\fad(180,180)}{\fs19\c&H9BCEE5&}MARA • RADIO{\rDialogue}\NStop the sequence. We need the rescue boat against the lower stairs.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:45.49,0:10:49.38,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\fad(180,180)}{\fs19\c&H9BCEE5&}RESCUE COORDINATOR • RADIO{\rDialogue}\NEight minutes if the approach is clear.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:49.38,0:10:52.88,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\fad(180,180)}{\fs19\c&H9BCEE5&}TOMAS{\rDialogue}\NI'm cold.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:52.88,0:11:00.62,Narrative,,0,0,0,,{\fad(180,180)}Leila sees the shelter counts downstream. She authorizes the remaining release. The boat arrives twelve minutes later.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:00.62,0:11:04.90,Narrative,,0,0,0,,{\fad(180,180)}Tomas dies before they can lift him aboard.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:08.90,0:11:17.41,Narrative,,0,0,0,,{\fad(180,180)}The plan keeps the pumps working long enough to prevent a larger disaster. It does not prevent every death.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:17.41,0:11:25.92,Narrative,,0,0,0,,{\fad(180,180)}No one cheers. Leila's authorization remains in the public log. She does not ask for it to be removed.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:29.92,0:11:38.04,Narrative,,0,0,0,,{\fad(180,180)}Arun testifies for eleven days. Leila is asked if she regrets delaying her brother's rescue. She says yes.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:38.04,0:11:41.93,Narrative,,0,0,0,,{\fad(180,180)}Would she make the same decision again?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:41.93,0:11:46.98,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\fad(180,180)}{\fs19\c&H9BCEE5&}LEILA{\rDialogue}\NI believe I had to. You should examine it anyway.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:46.98,0:11:55.87,Narrative,,0,0,0,,{\fad(180,180)}Concord survives as a smaller provider. Public counts can be challenged. Emergency powers gain expiration dates. The law changes unevenly.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:59.87,0:12:06.45,Narrative,,0,0,0,,{\fad(180,180)}Mara brings back the old radio. Tomas replaced its capacitors twice. Underneath, a note:
Dialogue: 0,0:12:06.45,0:12:11.88,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\fad(180,180)}{\fs19\c&H9BCEE5&}TOMAS • NOTE{\rDialogue}\NStill only receives. Ask her when she's going to fix that.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:11.88,0:12:18.85,Narrative,,0,0,0,,{\fad(180,180)}Mara places a soldering iron on the table. They work until midnight. Neither mentions forgiveness.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:18.85,0:12:22.36,Narrative,,0,0,0,,{\fad(180,180)}In the morning, the radio transmits.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:26.36,0:12:34.87,Narrative,,0,0,0,,{\fad(180,180)}The world grows older, warmer, more capable, still unequal. The sea keeps rising. Some districts give the river room.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:34.87,0:12:41.84,Narrative,,0,0,0,,{\fad(180,180)}The neighborhood owns its batteries. Its elected committee has just lost office for favoring relatives.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:41.84,0:12:45.34,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\fad(180,180)}{\fs19\c&H9BCEE5&}INA{\rDialogue}\NCan we see the boats?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:45.34,0:12:48.85,Narrative,,0,0,0,,{\fad(180,180)}They go to see the boats.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:52.85,0:12:57.51,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\fad(180,180)}{\fs19\c&H9BCEE5&}INA{\rDialogue}\NWhat did you think the future would look like?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:57.51,0:13:02.94,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\fad(180,180)}{\fs19\c&H9BCEE5&}LEILA{\rDialogue}\NCleaner. When I was young, the pictures were always very clean.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:02.94,0:13:06.44,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\fad(180,180)}{\fs19\c&H9BCEE5&}INA{\rDialogue}\NYou could clean this.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:06.44,0:13:09.94,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\fad(180,180)}{\fs19\c&H9BCEE5&}LEILA{\rDialogue}\NYes.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:09.94,0:13:17.29,Narrative,,0,0,0,,{\fad(180,180)}Ina fits the antenna and calls the repair boat. She asks how many people are aboard.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:17.29,0:13:20.79,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\fad(180,180)}{\fs19\c&H9BCEE5&}PILOT • RADIO{\rDialogue}\NSix. Seven with me.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:20.79,0:13:30.07,Narrative,,0,0,0,,{\fad(180,180)}She writes the number in the harbor watch book. Leila watches her do it. The boat's light crosses the dark water.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:30.07,0:13:39.35,Narrative,,0,0,0,,{\fad(180,180)}THE SHARE OF THE LIVING — Adapted from story/story.md. A fictional future, 2029–2100. Animation and original non-voice sound rendered with MYT.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:00.40,0:00:02.80,Title,,0,0,0,,{\fad(180,180)}The Share of the Living\N{\fs20}2029 — 2100
